WEBVTT

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:15.640
My right hand holds a bowl of gold,

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.180
And my left holds one of silver.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.720
Never one without the other,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:37.800
Two unseen bowls for each of us.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:46.210
The golden one is filled with joy,

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:53.550
shining warmly.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.350
Since we met, my golden bowl

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:05.360
cannot hold all my happiness and love.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:15.500
Golden joy, silver sadness,

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:22.850
I would leave my past behind...

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:27.580
For you, for the sake of love,

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:34.520
I would empty the bowls of my past.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:56.980
"Education?" <b> </b>

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:57.850
"Education?" <i>Kyouiku.</i>

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.390
Next: "polite"? <b> </b>

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:00.400
Next: "polite"? <i>Teinei-na.</i>

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:01.780
"Individual"? <b> </b>

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.850
"Individual"? <i>Tandoku-no, koko-no,dokutoku-no.</i>

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.390
"Trend?"

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.520
<i>Sonohou e muke, katamuku, hucho...</i>

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:10.460
"Unbecoming?" <b> </b>

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:12.390
"Unbecoming?" Hmmm? Mmmm...

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:14.130
<i>Niawa nai, husouou-na...</i> <b> </b>

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:15.530
<i>Niawa nai, husouou-na...</i> That's it!

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:21.940
She'll be back in school beginning today, Shinobu-san.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:23.380
Mmm?

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:27.540
Mid-terms are next week, and she feels much better.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:28.540
Mmm...

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:31.150
Why don't we have lunch together some time. The three of us.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:33.880
What do you say? <b> </b>

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:34.880
What do you say? I'll think about it!

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:38.420
My dear brother...

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:41.690
Shinonu Mariko-san is coming back to school.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:46.490
It was partly my fault,

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.560
and I can't say everything is going to be the same,

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:53.370
...but I'd rather that we forget all the unpleasant things,

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:57.720
...and concentrate on these coming mid-terms instead.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:08.520
Stop the car! Right here is fine.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.330
Take this.

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:22.190
The one you wanted, a Jean Saint-Teauille first edition...

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:26.670
But it's so precious, you said you'd never part with it...

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:30.070
You'd prefer I weren't so... changeable?

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:33.940
No...

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:46.010
<b>11. Under the Elm Tree</b>

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:59.540
Sorority members: please assemble at the Sorority House at once.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:07.780
Look! Sorority members!

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:10.110
They're going to the Sorority House...! <b> </b>

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:11.980
They're going to the Sorority House...! They'll study there for the midterms.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:16.790
The senior members always help the junior members study.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.390
They're so lucky. <b> </b>

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:19.450
They're so lucky. I'm envious!

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:29.130
As you know, mid-terms start next week.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:36.000
The Sorority expects all our new members to do well, of course.

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:42.280
This will be the first major exam for our new members...

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:48.350
...and I must remind you that our rules require that you place in the top 50.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:50.290
The top 50!

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.760
But there is nothing to worry about.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:57.360
Our senior members are here to help our junior members study.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.500
This is our Sorority's tradition.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.770
Perhaps you'd like to see the kind of questions...

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:05.390
...you can expect to find in Seiran's exams...?

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:11.310
We'll start this afternoon.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:16.780
Since it is the first day, we'll meet at my house.

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:20.410
We can enjoy tea and study.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:27.870
How wonderful to be able to go to Miya-sama's house!

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:29.560
I'll see you all this afternoon.

00:05:37.010 --> 00:05:37.950
Shinobu-san...?

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:39.610
Yes?

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:42.400
You were hospitalized recently...?

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:44.500
Yes.

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:49.280
Don't forget that being healthy is another requirement of the Sorority.

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:50.810
Yes.

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:53.690
But, I'm glad your hospitalization was a short one.

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:56.350
Thank you very much.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:58.870
It may start raining...

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:09.230
It was so beautiful this morning.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:01.550
Is Jean Saint-Teauille to your liking?

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:03.350
Yes!

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:06.820
Sorority members are getting together at my house today.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:08.960
Do you want to come?

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:10.630
To my house?

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:12.560
To your house?

00:07:13.230 --> 00:07:15.170
Yes, to my house.

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:22.110
I will take you to my house.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:29.650
Wait for me at five o'clock under the elm tree in the court yard.

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:33.530
All right?

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:07.690
After school, all junior members were divided into groups.

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:09.490
We got into the senior members's cars...

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:12.160
...and headed to Fukiko-sama's house.

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:17.030
The darkened sky seemed ready to shed raindrops like tears.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:23.300
Though I was excited, I also felt somewhat anxious and uneasy.

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:27.510
Perhaps I was feeling a premonition of the unforgettable event...

00:08:27.510 --> 00:08:30.480
...which was about to unfold before me.

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:48.260
Please do come in.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:51.680
We'll be serving tea and cakes.

00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:01.870
Yes, this <i>"Nubatama-no"</i> is a <i>Makura Kotoba</i> modifying "night".

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:04.940
<i>Makura Kotoba</i> will be covered on the mid-term.

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:08.880
Yes, this requires factoring.

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:11.280
Underline in red the rule on page 90 of your text book.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:13.020
It's an important point.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:24.830
<i>Haru sugite, natsu kitarurashi shirotae no,</i>

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:27.430
<i>...koromo hoshi tari, ame no kaguyama.</i>

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:31.260
You must not only memorize this poem,

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:33.620
but make sure you understand the meaning also.

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:48.590
<i>Imasara ni, nanioka omowan uchinabiki,</i>

00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:51.120
<i>...kokoro wa kimi ni yorinishimono wo.</i>

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:54.790
Good. Next, the Spring Poem by Ootomo Yakamochi?

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:58.730
<i>Uchikirashi yuki wa furutsutsu shikasuga ni,</i>

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:01.200
<i>...wagie no sono ni uguisu naku.</i>

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:17.550
<i>Omouni shi, shinisuru mono ni aramaseba</i>

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:20.500
<i>...chikabito warera shini kaerabashi.</i>

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:26.430
Wow, it's raining hard...!

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:28.960
Continue, Misonoo-san...

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:33.230
<i>Yamino yo wa kurushiki mono wo itsushika to</i>

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:36.200
<i>...ana matsu tsukini haya mo teranuka.</i>

00:10:55.430 --> 00:10:56.920
What's wrong, Nanako-san?

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:00.460
What's the matter, Misonoo-san?

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:06.870
Oh my, I'm sorry... I left my French reading book and notebook at school!

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:08.930
I'll go back to pick them up!

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:11.200
But it's raining.

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:14.820
Suppose we study mathematics instead of French today...

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:18.910
Yes, but I have a homework due tomorrow, and I need my notebook...

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:23.280
Well... Then I'll have my driver take you there.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:26.290
I won't hear of it! It's OK - I'll be right back.

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:33.960
Darn! I've forgotten my umbrella...

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:36.100
Take this.

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:40.170
Thank you! I'm very grateful...

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:42.770
Rain during this season is very cold.

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:44.500
Thank you very much!

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:52.240
Did you see that? Miya-sama lavishes her attention on Misonoo-san.

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:53.450
Yeah...

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:57.250
Even the studying - Miya-sama has been teaching only Misonoo-san.

00:11:57.450 --> 00:11:59.320
Do you think it's true? <b> </b>

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:00.080
Do you think it's true? "It"?

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:00.920
Do you think it's true? "It"? What "It"?

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:07.260
The rumour that it was Miya-sama alone who insisted that Misonoo-san be chosen.

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:08.590
Hold it, what do you mean... <b> </b>

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:09.730
Hold it, what do you mean... Everyone...

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:13.470
Let's take another break for tea.

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:48.570
That song... it's the one Saint-Juste is always playing...

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:26.410
Here it is!

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:54.100
Exhaustion and relief, combined with the steady soothing sound of raindrops,

00:13:54.300 --> 00:14:01.110
...made the classroom feel like a quiet haven at the bottom of the sea...

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:22.530
But now it was dark outside - I had been asleep over an hour.

00:14:24.270 --> 00:14:26.470
Oh, no! I've got to go back!

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:54.700
Saint-Juste...!

00:15:05.310 --> 00:15:06.710
Saint-Juste-sama!

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:11.250
Saint-Juste-sama!

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:25.790
Saint-Juste-sama! Saint-Juste-sama!

00:15:27.930 --> 00:15:30.730
You're soaking! You'll catch a cold, Saint-Juste-sama!

00:15:30.870 --> 00:15:32.200
What are you doing here?

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:38.810
Why was she there, wet and alone under that elm tree...?

00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:45.680
...I had no idea then. And what could she be thinking...

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:51.550
She was cold as ice, soaked to the bone, and couldn't even talk.

00:15:54.360 --> 00:15:59.430
So I took her to her home, using the address on her student ID.

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:02.430
Saint-Juste-sama, are you OK?

00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:04.630
Snap out of it! Come to your senses!

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:07.100
Itlu-chome, you said?

00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:10.510
Yes! 1-17-15 Maison d'Eduard.

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:20.180
Saint-Juste-sama!

00:16:20.720 --> 00:16:23.520
I'm taking you to your home.

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:28.190
Fukiko-sama...

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:31.060
I was to wait there..!

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:34.400
...wait... for Fukiko-sama!

00:16:44.010 --> 00:16:45.470
Whaddaya think you're doing..!!? <b> </b>

00:16:45.470 --> 00:16:47.210
Whaddaya think you're doing..!!? I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:52.010
Watch out!

00:16:53.480 --> 00:16:54.820
I'm leaving you here!

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:57.950
I don't need this kind of trouble!

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:01.490
Saint-Juste-sama!

00:17:03.490 --> 00:17:04.560
I need to get back.

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:06.630
To the elm tree.

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:12.700
Saint-Juste-sama!

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:16.570
That's the opposite direction from your home!

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:24.580
I must go.

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:27.120
To where?

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:31.120
She's... feverish!

00:17:32.390 --> 00:17:33.920
I must get back...

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:37.330
No, you mustn't! You have a fever!

00:17:37.330 --> 00:17:39.930
You need to go home! Please go home!

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:42.330
Otherwise... otherwise I'll...

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:46.000
Saint-Juste-sama!

00:17:51.210 --> 00:17:53.340
Please! Please wait!!

00:18:21.170 --> 00:18:23.040
Yes, sweet peas...

00:18:24.770 --> 00:18:26.040
Thank you very much.

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:39.790
I'll... I'll give these to you...

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:46.600
So... don't pay any mind to me... anymore.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:49.130
Thanks.

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:51.330
Saint-Juste-sama!

00:19:12.220 --> 00:19:15.560
I can't make Kukiko-sama wait.

00:19:16.490 --> 00:19:17.560
Miya-sama?

00:19:17.560 --> 00:19:19.760
She's going to take me to her home.

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:25.100
She told me to wait. At 5 o'clock. Under the elm tree.

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:30.840
But... but Miya-sama...

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:34.110
But Miya-sama is already at her home!

00:19:50.930 --> 00:19:52.460
You're a bad girl.

00:19:53.660 --> 00:19:55.200
Such a liar...!

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:56.670
That was no lie!

00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:07.340
I must hurry...

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:12.350
Fukiko-sama... Fukiko-sama, I'm coming right now...

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:18.290
NO!

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:45.450
Don't... Saint-Juste-sama... you mustn't...

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:19.420
Is this the place?

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:29.160
No... wait... I'll open it.

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:45.510
I'll do it!

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:48.720
OK...

00:22:16.470 --> 00:22:17.410
Mirrors?

00:22:19.540 --> 00:22:22.280
Mirrors...and so many of them!

00:22:27.420 --> 00:22:29.490
Where is everyone?

00:22:30.090 --> 00:22:31.890
"Everyone"?

00:22:42.370 --> 00:22:44.370
There is no "everyone" here.

00:22:45.900 --> 00:22:46.970
Alone?

00:22:48.370 --> 00:22:51.980
She lives here alone, surrounded by mirrors?

00:22:53.980 --> 00:22:56.050
Ma cherie La Poupee...

00:22:56.650 --> 00:22:59.050
Where's the bathroom? Where is it?

00:22:59.250 --> 00:23:02.520
You have to dry off and change right now! Which way is it?

00:23:03.990 --> 00:23:06.790
Ma cherie La Poupee....

00:23:27.610 --> 00:23:30.080
Ma cherie La Poupee...

00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:14.360
I dreamed I was chasing a rainbow...

00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:19.830
Then the rainbow I was chasing was you.

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:25.440
Before, I had no strength, no will.

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:30.910
But now because of you, I do.

00:24:31.650 --> 00:24:37.190
Feelings of love, like raindrops

00:24:37.190 --> 00:24:42.660
Come pouring from the sky.

00:24:42.660 --> 00:24:45.390
This is surely a game

00:24:45.390 --> 00:24:48.200
Of some mischievous fairy...

00:24:48.200 --> 00:24:50.600
Always dancing,

00:24:50.600 --> 00:24:55.870
Always capricious...

00:25:02.040 --> 00:25:04.840
Preview

00:25:04.840 --> 00:25:09.920
Kaoru-no-Kimi arrives at Rei's apartment...

00:25:10.180 --> 00:25:12.850
She slaps Rei and angrily rips the bracelet from her wrist!

00:25:14.320 --> 00:25:18.390
And Nanako can now see what was concealed beneath the bracelet...

00:25:19.860 --> 00:25:20.930
Next episode: <b> </b>

00:25:20.930 --> 00:25:22.600
Next episode: <b>The Scar</b>

00:25:22.730 --> 00:25:24.320
Brother, Dear Brother... <b> </b>

00:25:24.320 --> 00:25:28.740
Brother, Dear Brother... There is no end to my tears...
